WEBVTT

00:00:02.310 --> 00:00:06.940
Project Mew, an operation to search for Mew,
is underway.

00:00:07.690 --> 00:00:13.910
Go, who hopes to join the search,
must clear various Pokémon-related Trial Missions.

00:00:15.700 --> 00:00:18.870
Every successfully cleared mission
nets the participant a token.

00:00:18.870 --> 00:00:22.620
The three candidates who obtain
the most tokens will be accepted.

00:00:23.790 --> 00:00:30.170
Will Go be able to join the official Mew search team,
and become a Chaser?

00:00:31.510 --> 00:00:32.670
It’s here!

00:00:32.670 --> 00:00:34.130
A Trial Mission!

00:00:34.130 --> 00:00:35.430
Let me see...

00:00:35.430 --> 00:00:39.760
“Reach the goal by using
your ingenuity and imagination.”

00:00:39.760 --> 00:00:42.390
I can choose from
three missions again, too!

00:00:42.390 --> 00:00:43.390
What’re you gonna pick?

00:00:43.390 --> 00:00:46.560
Hmm... Good question...

00:00:47.560 --> 00:00:48.480
This one!

00:00:48.480 --> 00:00:50.980
“Catch a wild Kingdra!”

00:00:50.980 --> 00:00:52.570
A Kingdra, huh?

00:00:52.570 --> 00:00:55.280
I can catch Pokémon
better than anyone, yeah?!

00:00:56.200 --> 00:00:57.870
You’re very confident today.

00:00:57.870 --> 00:01:01.160
Go, take a look at
the main monitor.

00:01:01.740 --> 00:01:05.960
Kingdra. Dragon Pokémon.
Water/Dragon type.

00:01:05.960 --> 00:01:09.500
Kingdra lives at extreme ocean depths
that are otherwise uninhabited.

00:01:09.500 --> 00:01:13.380
It is said to create whirlpools
by yawning.

00:01:13.380 --> 00:01:17.010
When a Kingdra and a Kairyu meet,
a fierce battle ensues.

00:01:17.010 --> 00:01:21.810
Catching a wild Kingdra
is known to be pretty difficult.

00:01:21.810 --> 00:01:26.940
Which is why the most common method
of getting one is by trade evolution,

00:01:26.940 --> 00:01:29.400
by having a Seadra
hold a Dragon Scale and trading it.

00:01:29.400 --> 00:01:31.980
Sounds like it won’t be
a straightforward task.

00:01:32.730 --> 00:01:33.650
You sure about this?

00:01:34.880 --> 00:01:36.030
Uhh...

00:01:36.860 --> 00:01:38.280
You’ll be fine!

00:01:38.280 --> 00:01:40.530
You can catch Pokémon
better than anyone, right?

00:01:40.530 --> 00:01:42.240
Y-Yeah!

00:01:42.790 --> 00:01:44.500
Then, let’s get to it...

00:01:44.500 --> 00:01:49.420
Seadra habitats could also be home
to their evolution, Kingdra.

00:01:49.790 --> 00:01:50.960
That’s right!

00:01:52.460 --> 00:01:53.710
Here we go!

00:01:53.710 --> 00:01:57.630
The seas near Hoenn’s Kaina City!
There have even been whirlpool sightings!

00:01:57.630 --> 00:02:00.640
Okay, then, off to Hoenn...

00:02:01.010 --> 00:02:02.970
Let’s go!

00:03:41.650 --> 00:03:45.320
Hoenn Region, here we are!

00:03:45.620 --> 00:03:47.290
We can go the rest of the way
on our Pokémon!

00:03:47.290 --> 00:03:48.120
Okay!

00:03:48.120 --> 00:03:50.080
Come on out!

00:03:59.880 --> 00:04:01.880
Satoshi, it’s straight ahead!

00:04:01.880 --> 00:04:04.300
Tamanta, Dewgong, you’re up!

00:04:08.390 --> 00:04:09.600
All right!

00:04:09.600 --> 00:04:11.310
Let’s take a look around here.

00:04:11.310 --> 00:04:12.480
Okay!

00:04:14.480 --> 00:04:15.860
One, two...

00:04:31.000 --> 00:04:34.370
Lovecus! Rendezvous Pokémon!
Water type!

00:04:34.370 --> 00:04:37.080
Lovecus makes its home
in coral reefs in warm seas!

00:04:37.080 --> 00:04:41.130
It especially likes sleeping in
the space between Sunnygo’s branches!

00:05:13.620 --> 00:05:15.290
Never mind Kingdra...

00:05:15.290 --> 00:05:17.790
There’s not even any Seadra.

00:05:18.170 --> 00:05:21.300
Guess we’ll have to dive deeper...

00:05:21.300 --> 00:05:22.300
Yeah.

00:05:23.460 --> 00:05:25.260
One, two...

00:06:16.560 --> 00:06:19.190
What are you doing
messing around out here?!

00:06:23.610 --> 00:06:25.110
Is that...?

00:06:26.740 --> 00:06:27.900
Mr. Gonji!

00:06:27.900 --> 00:06:29.070
It’s Genji!

00:06:29.530 --> 00:06:32.830
Mr. Genji...
From the Hoenn Elite Four?!

00:06:32.830 --> 00:06:34.160
Mm-hmm.

00:06:35.950 --> 00:06:38.250
And your name, was it...
Sabashi?

00:06:39.040 --> 00:06:40.830
Satoshi...

00:06:42.500 --> 00:06:43.590
Oh?

00:06:43.590 --> 00:06:45.710
A wild Kingdra?

00:06:45.710 --> 00:06:48.840
Yes. Have you seen any
around here?

00:06:48.840 --> 00:06:49.840
I have!

00:06:49.840 --> 00:06:50.760
Really?

00:06:50.760 --> 00:06:51.590
Where?!

00:06:51.930 --> 00:06:59.310
One time when I was already deep underwater,
I was caught in a whirlpool, and dragged down even deeper.

00:06:59.310 --> 00:07:03.810
That’s the one and only time
I’ve seen a wild Kingdra.

00:07:04.190 --> 00:07:08.110
Sounds like it’s way deeper than
we ourselves could dive, then...

00:07:08.110 --> 00:07:11.490
We’ve just gotta try harder,
and dive down deeper!

00:07:11.490 --> 00:07:15.080
No matter how hard you try,
some things just aren’t possible!

00:07:15.080 --> 00:07:17.160
Gonna give up, then?

00:07:17.160 --> 00:07:18.620
No way!

00:07:18.620 --> 00:07:21.040
I just need to think
if there’s some way to...

00:07:21.670 --> 00:07:22.290
Huh?

00:07:22.920 --> 00:07:23.790
What is it?

00:07:24.250 --> 00:07:27.170
The preface to today’s mission.

00:07:27.170 --> 00:07:30.930
“Reach the goal by using
your ingenuity and imagination.”

00:07:30.930 --> 00:07:32.470
Yeah, that was it!

00:07:32.470 --> 00:07:34.140
So, then...

00:07:34.680 --> 00:07:38.140
Mr. Genji,
when you dove down before...

00:07:38.560 --> 00:07:40.100
I’ve heard enough.

00:07:40.100 --> 00:07:41.440
Very well.

00:07:41.440 --> 00:07:43.150
I can lend you my equipment.

00:07:44.060 --> 00:07:45.560
You did it, Go!

00:07:45.560 --> 00:07:47.150
However!

00:07:47.530 --> 00:07:50.240
You have to help out
with my work.

00:07:50.240 --> 00:07:51.650
Work?

00:07:51.650 --> 00:07:53.780
Treasure hunting!

00:07:57.280 --> 00:07:59.540
Keep it coming, keep it coming...

00:08:00.450 --> 00:08:01.790
Ahem, ahem...

00:08:01.790 --> 00:08:03.120
Mr. Genji...

00:08:03.120 --> 00:08:04.580
How’s it going?

00:08:04.580 --> 00:08:07.170
No problems yet.

00:08:07.550 --> 00:08:11.800
An ancient submarine
from thousands of years ago, huh?

00:08:11.800 --> 00:08:14.140
It’d be incredible if we found it!

00:08:14.140 --> 00:08:15.220
Yeah!

00:08:15.220 --> 00:08:18.060
It feels like we’re wasting time
just standing around here.

00:08:18.060 --> 00:08:19.930
Satoshi, get Lucario out!

00:08:19.930 --> 00:08:21.680
Huh? Sure, I guess...

00:08:25.900 --> 00:08:28.520
Chonchie can send
Supersonic Waves into the sea.

00:08:29.730 --> 00:08:34.410
So I’d like you to use Lucario’s Aura
to investigate what it picks up.

00:08:34.410 --> 00:08:35.610
I get it!

00:08:35.610 --> 00:08:37.490
Pokémon Radar!

00:08:37.490 --> 00:08:39.290
Lucario, you up for it?

00:08:59.430 --> 00:09:01.720
The sun’ll be setting soon.

00:09:02.270 --> 00:09:04.600
Should we call it quits for today?

00:09:04.980 --> 00:09:05.850
Yeah!

00:09:08.190 --> 00:09:09.400
What is it?

00:09:09.400 --> 00:09:11.070
Did you find something?

00:09:14.990 --> 00:09:18.950
Mr. Genji! Keep heading toward
the setting sun!

00:09:18.950 --> 00:09:20.620
There might be something there!

00:09:20.620 --> 00:09:22.160
Mm-hmm. Got it.

00:09:25.750 --> 00:09:26.870
Anything there?

00:09:26.870 --> 00:09:28.750
No, nothing of note.

00:09:28.750 --> 00:09:29.840
Hmm...?

00:09:29.840 --> 00:09:31.340
Hold on...

00:09:36.970 --> 00:09:39.470
Oh! Here it is!

00:09:39.470 --> 00:09:41.470
It’s the ancient submarine.

00:09:41.470 --> 00:09:42.770
What?!

00:09:42.770 --> 00:09:46.520
Plus, it’s shaped like a Kingdra.

00:09:46.520 --> 00:09:47.940
A Kingdra?

00:09:47.940 --> 00:09:50.650
It definitely wasn’t here before...

00:09:50.650 --> 00:09:53.650
But it’s too dangerous to stay out
if it gets any darker.

00:09:53.650 --> 00:09:56.030
Let’s hold off until tomorrow.

00:09:56.030 --> 00:09:57.530
Bring me back!

00:09:57.530 --> 00:09:58.820
Right!

00:10:00.990 --> 00:10:03.540
That was delicious...
That was a great meal...

00:10:10.170 --> 00:10:12.090
It’s so sweet and tasty!

00:10:12.090 --> 00:10:13.300
Naturally.

00:10:13.300 --> 00:10:16.090
That’s my Hot Moomoo Milk.

00:10:16.090 --> 00:10:18.050
But forget about that.
Give this a look.

00:10:18.840 --> 00:10:21.050
So that’s the
ancient submarine...

00:10:21.050 --> 00:10:23.390
But why is it shaped
like a Kingdra?

00:10:23.390 --> 00:10:24.890
No idea.

00:10:24.890 --> 00:10:31.020
But it seems the ancient civilization
behind the submarine idolized Kingdra.

00:10:32.650 --> 00:10:33.520
What’s that?

00:10:33.520 --> 00:10:34.900
Oh...

00:10:34.900 --> 00:10:39.410
When I was walking Komoru,
I happened to find this vase on the beach.

00:10:39.410 --> 00:10:44.030
I looked into it, and found
there’s a legend told about these waters.

00:10:44.030 --> 00:10:50.040
Apparently, an ancient submarine sunk here,
with treasure aboard.

00:10:50.040 --> 00:10:56.590
Since then, I picked up treasure hunting as a hobby,
whenever I’m not busy with Elite Four duties.

00:10:56.590 --> 00:10:58.260
You don’t say...

00:10:58.260 --> 00:11:03.930
Once, I had a huge sailboat...
But this small ship works just as well.

00:11:03.930 --> 00:11:06.060
Oh, that reminds me....

00:11:06.060 --> 00:11:07.640
I found this in the sea...

00:11:07.640 --> 00:11:08.310
Mm-hmm.

00:11:08.310 --> 00:11:10.600
That’s it, exactly.

00:11:10.600 --> 00:11:12.310
You’re pretty lucky yourselves.

00:11:12.310 --> 00:11:15.230
You even found
the whole sub, after all.

00:11:18.440 --> 00:11:22.320
But, Mr. Genji... What’re you gonna do
after you find the treasure?

00:11:22.740 --> 00:11:24.330
Look for the next one.

00:11:24.330 --> 00:11:25.410
Huh?

00:11:25.410 --> 00:11:27.450
You’d just move on, that easily?

00:11:27.450 --> 00:11:28.450
Hmph!

00:11:28.450 --> 00:11:31.460
What I’m really looking for
are dreams and adventures.

00:11:32.710 --> 00:11:34.840
That’s so cool!

00:11:35.710 --> 00:11:37.170
Okay, we have an early day in store.

00:11:37.170 --> 00:11:38.210
Let’s get to sleep!

00:11:38.210 --> 00:11:39.050
Right!

00:11:42.840 --> 00:11:43.640
Huh?

00:11:43.640 --> 00:11:45.720
You want me and Satoshi to dive?

00:11:45.720 --> 00:11:46.760
I do.

00:11:46.760 --> 00:11:48.270
But... are you sure?

00:11:48.270 --> 00:11:50.680
You’ve been looking for the treasure
for so long...

00:11:50.680 --> 00:11:53.310
It’s your turn to
have your dreams come true.

00:11:53.770 --> 00:11:56.610
Go catch that wild Kingdra!

00:11:56.610 --> 00:11:57.570
Right!

00:12:05.320 --> 00:12:08.620
If the ancient people
used Kingdra as their crest,

00:12:08.620 --> 00:12:11.460
we might find some hint
in the submarine!

00:12:11.460 --> 00:12:14.120
All right! Let’s start
by searching the sub!

00:12:14.120 --> 00:12:14.830
Yeah!

00:12:14.830 --> 00:12:17.040
Take these with you!

00:12:18.090 --> 00:12:21.970
Even if your hose should fall off,
these will let you breathe for ten minutes.

00:12:22.630 --> 00:12:24.260
Thank you!

00:12:43.700 --> 00:12:44.490
There it is...

00:12:45.320 --> 00:12:47.780
The ancient submarine!

00:13:01.960 --> 00:13:04.130
We’re heading for the submarine.

00:13:04.130 --> 00:13:06.430
Be very careful out there.

00:13:13.020 --> 00:13:14.020
What’s wrong?

00:13:14.020 --> 00:13:16.310
There’s a really strong current...!

00:13:16.310 --> 00:13:17.600
A current?

00:13:17.600 --> 00:13:18.900
I get it...

00:13:18.900 --> 00:13:24.650
The submarine wasn’t always there.
I suppose the current must have carried it here.

00:13:25.150 --> 00:13:26.780
That can happen...?!

00:13:26.780 --> 00:13:28.450
Go, let’s go!

00:13:28.450 --> 00:13:29.410
Right!

00:13:52.140 --> 00:13:53.970
A Huntail!

00:13:53.970 --> 00:13:56.270
And there’s a Sakurabyss!

00:13:56.890 --> 00:13:58.520
And now, a Seadra.

00:13:58.520 --> 00:14:00.860
<i>Seadra!</i>

00:14:01.520 --> 00:14:04.110
H-Hold on!

00:14:06.200 --> 00:14:07.910
What is it?

00:14:07.910 --> 00:14:10.120
I saw a Seadra, but I lost it...

00:14:25.090 --> 00:14:26.920
A Jilanth...

00:14:29.890 --> 00:14:31.050
You okay?

00:14:32.010 --> 00:14:33.140
Yeah!

00:14:34.560 --> 00:14:35.850
What’s that...?

00:14:38.350 --> 00:14:40.060
A treasure chest?!

00:14:41.020 --> 00:14:44.070
Maybe you’ll find a hint inside.

00:14:47.320 --> 00:14:49.110
It’s just mud...

00:14:49.110 --> 00:14:50.860
We shouldn’t give up yet.

00:14:55.490 --> 00:14:57.120
A scale?

00:14:57.120 --> 00:14:59.870
It’s blue, and it’s really pretty.

00:14:59.870 --> 00:15:03.250
That might just be a Dragon Scale.

00:15:03.250 --> 00:15:07.590
That reminds me,
if you have a Seadra hold a Dragon Scale...

00:15:10.800 --> 00:15:11.510
Seadra?

00:15:11.970 --> 00:15:13.350
Okay, time to catc—

00:15:25.440 --> 00:15:29.280
Samehada’s data will be
added to the Index!

00:15:29.280 --> 00:15:30.490
Whaaa?!

00:15:34.200 --> 00:15:36.660
Do you want this?

00:15:37.950 --> 00:15:40.870
You could evolve
into a Kingdra, after all.

00:15:40.870 --> 00:15:42.790
Here, a present.

00:15:44.540 --> 00:15:45.500
You sure?

00:15:45.500 --> 00:15:46.590
Yeah.

00:15:46.590 --> 00:15:50.630
My mission was
to catch a wild Kingdra.

00:15:50.630 --> 00:15:53.720
Hey, do you know
where I might find this guy?

00:15:56.350 --> 00:15:58.100
Are you showing us the way?

00:16:11.950 --> 00:16:15.120
Mr. Genji!
We want to dive down deeper!

00:16:15.120 --> 00:16:17.080
It can’t go any deeper.

00:16:18.200 --> 00:16:19.750
Go, look!

00:16:21.750 --> 00:16:24.290
Is it in that cave?!

00:16:28.420 --> 00:16:30.880
What’s wrong, Seadra?!

00:16:36.720 --> 00:16:38.140
What now?

00:16:38.720 --> 00:16:40.470
It’s a whirlpool!

00:16:40.470 --> 00:16:41.390
I’m pulling you back up!

00:16:41.390 --> 00:16:42.890
Please, hold on...

00:16:42.890 --> 00:16:45.020
Kingdra could be doing this!

00:16:45.020 --> 00:16:46.270
What?!

00:16:46.810 --> 00:16:50.770
The Index even says Kingdra
creates whirlpools by yawning!

00:16:51.440 --> 00:16:52.570
True...

00:16:52.570 --> 00:16:54.030
I’m going to take a look.

00:16:54.030 --> 00:16:56.240
Satoshi, you wait for me here!

00:16:56.240 --> 00:16:59.160
Huh? Wait for you?!

00:17:21.680 --> 00:17:26.650
I thought if I let the whirlpool draw me in,
it might take me to Kingdra.

00:17:26.650 --> 00:17:28.520
Do I wait for another whirlpool?

00:17:29.360 --> 00:17:31.320
No, I don’t have time...

00:17:32.360 --> 00:17:37.280
Oh, when a Kingdra and a Kairyu meet,
a fierce battle ensues!

00:17:51.000 --> 00:17:52.550
There it is, a Kingdra!

00:17:57.970 --> 00:17:59.300
What now...?

00:17:59.300 --> 00:18:02.100
Throwing a Monster Ball
doesn’t work underwater...

00:18:03.720 --> 00:18:06.430
I know! You’re up!

00:18:09.190 --> 00:18:10.310
Snipe Shot!

00:18:13.530 --> 00:18:15.280
Keep firing Snipe Shots!

00:18:22.530 --> 00:18:24.370
Dragon Breath?!

00:18:25.410 --> 00:18:27.870
Am I no match for it underwater...?!

00:18:29.920 --> 00:18:31.500
Satoshi! Uonoragon!

00:18:31.500 --> 00:18:34.960
We’re here for you!
Don’t give up!

00:18:34.960 --> 00:18:37.420
Right! I have my friends with me!

00:18:37.420 --> 00:18:39.510
Come on out, Tamanta!

00:18:41.890 --> 00:18:45.030
Use Ice Beam around Kingdra!

00:18:54.980 --> 00:18:56.230
Okay, Inteleon!

00:18:56.230 --> 00:18:58.320
Let’s use the move
that we’ve been practicing!

00:18:58.320 --> 00:18:59.570
Aqua Break!

00:19:08.060 --> 00:19:09.040
All right...

00:19:09.040 --> 00:19:10.960
Snipe Shot!

00:19:19.760 --> 00:19:21.430
We did it!

00:19:21.430 --> 00:19:24.930
Kingdra’s data will be
added to the Index!

00:19:38.530 --> 00:19:40.070
Oh no, my oxygen...!

00:19:40.070 --> 00:19:42.360
I need you to help me out!

00:19:45.120 --> 00:19:47.370
Satoshi, hold onto Kingdra!

00:19:47.370 --> 00:19:48.700
Okay!

00:19:48.700 --> 00:19:50.210
We’re gonna make
a quick escape!

00:19:50.210 --> 00:19:52.330
Kingdra! Dragon Breath!

00:20:01.680 --> 00:20:03.340
Seadra?

00:20:22.400 --> 00:20:26.070
I’ve verified your capture
of a wild Kingdra.

00:20:26.070 --> 00:20:27.450
Well done.

00:20:27.450 --> 00:20:28.910
Thank you!

00:20:30.200 --> 00:20:31.910
Asahi, hurry it up!

00:20:32.540 --> 00:20:34.210
Don’t you boss me around.

00:20:35.960 --> 00:20:37.000
It’s coming.

00:20:38.250 --> 00:20:39.960
So, we finally meet.

00:20:45.720 --> 00:20:47.300
I’ve been waiting for this.

00:20:47.300 --> 00:20:50.060
The Legendary Pokémon,
Regirock.

00:20:58.150 --> 00:21:00.400
All right! The token is here!

00:21:01.490 --> 00:21:03.530
Now you’ve got two!

00:21:03.530 --> 00:21:05.610
I’ve <i>finally</i> got two, you mean!

00:21:05.610 --> 00:21:12.450
So Go, you’re collecting those token things
and trying to join a Mew search project.

00:21:12.450 --> 00:21:13.250
Right.

00:21:13.910 --> 00:21:20.920
And Satoshi, you entered the Championships,
aiming to become the world’s strongest Pokémon Trainer.

00:21:20.920 --> 00:21:21.760
Yeah?

00:21:22.460 --> 00:21:24.590
Now <i>there’s</i> dreams and adventures.

00:21:24.590 --> 00:21:27.050
You kids’ve gotta hold onto those!

00:21:28.390 --> 00:21:32.060
I’ll be chasing dreams and adventures
for the rest of my life, too!

00:21:33.810 --> 00:21:37.650
Go passed his second Trial Mission
with flying colors.

00:21:37.650 --> 00:21:42.650
However, his next mission has
an even tougher task in store.

00:23:07.190 --> 00:23:09.610
Now! Onto the next adventure!

00:23:09.610 --> 00:23:10.910
Go!

00:23:11.660 --> 00:23:13.620
Hikari’s Pochama was kidnapped?!

00:23:13.620 --> 00:23:15.340
Satoshi! Let’s check it out!

00:23:15.340 --> 00:23:16.160
Let’s go!

00:23:16.160 --> 00:23:17.200
Commence attack.

00:23:17.200 --> 00:23:18.910
Evil Pulse!

00:23:18.910 --> 00:23:19.750
Captured.

00:23:19.750 --> 00:23:20.250
Lucario!

00:23:20.250 --> 00:23:21.370
Inteleon!

00:23:21.370 --> 00:23:25.500
You and I are the same person,
living in different worlds.

00:23:25.500 --> 00:23:28.590
That might be an entrance
to another world.

00:23:28.590 --> 00:23:30.340
Next time, on Pocket Monsters:

00:23:30.340 --> 00:23:34.050
Dialga & Palkia!
The Space-Time Cataclysm!!
